<div id="services-offerings-containter" class="content-padding">
    <div id="services-offering-container">
        <ul>
            <li>
                <div class="photo" id="offering-1"></div>
                <h2>Epoxy Coatings</h2>
                <p>These epoxy-based industrial coatings are highly durable and resistant to chemicals, abrasion, and impact, making them ideal for floors, tanks, and pipelines.</p>
            </li>

            <li>
                <div class="photo" id="offering-2"></div>
                <h2>Polyurethane Coatings</h2>
                <p>These coatings are known for flexibility and UV resistance, protecting surfaces from weathering. They’re often used on exterior surfaces and equipment.</p>
            </li>

            <li>
                <div class="photo" id="offering-3"></div>
                <h2>Zinc-Rich Coatings</h2>
                <p>Often used as primers, these zinc coatings provide excellent corrosion resistance, especially for steel structures—thanks to their use of zinc as a sacrificial metal.</p>
            </li>

            <li>
                <div class="photo" id="offering-4"></div>
                <h2>Intumescent Coatings</h2>
                <p>These fireproof coatings expand when exposed to high temperatures, forming an insulating layer to protect structural components from fire damage.</p>
            </li>

            <li>
                <div class="photo" id="offering-5"></div>
                <h2>Acrylic Coatings</h2>
                <p>These coatings are valued for their fast-drying properties and UV stability, making them suitable for outdoor applications where environmental exposure is a concern.</p>
            </li>

            <li>
                <div class="photo" id="offering-6"></div>
                <h2>Ceramic Coatings</h2>
                <p>Ceramic industrial coatings provide excellent thermal resistance and are often used to protect equipment exposed to high temperatures, like boilers, furnaces, and other heating components.</p>
            </li>

            <li>
                <div class="photo" id="offering-7"></div>
                <h2>Anti-Fouling Coatings</h2>
                <p>Often applied on surfaces exposed to water, these coatings prevent the buildup of biological materials like algae and barnacles. They’re often used in marine and offshore industries..</p>
            </li>

            <li>
                <div class="photo" id="offering-8"></div>
                <h2>Building Envelope Coatings</h2>
                <p>These coatings create a seamless barrier that helps resist moisture, corrosion, and temperature-related wear, making them ideal for exposed building surfaces.</p>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>